  I'm betting you'll care if you run out.  And the AoY increases
mana use by up to three times.  Rangers can only get to basic
in escape spells, so the spell won't do you any more good than
jumping boots (Unless you're burdened.  Don't be burdened on the
Astral Planes.)

  Haste self:
   - is an escape spell.
   - Makes you just as fast as boots/potion of speed.
   - Can be cast ahead of time.
   - Can be "pumped up".
   - You can drop the amulet of Yendor when you cast it.

  Haste self and the unlimited jumping from jumping boots is
the approach I've taken even with my Wizards with 1000+ Pwr
and skilled+ plus in every spell school.  An ordinary tool
source of light lets you take full advantage of the range
of jumping boots.

  Add a wand of teleport when necessary and the planes of Earth,
Fire, and Astral just fly by.  And on the Astral Plane traveling 
speed is even more important because you may spend a lot of time 
backtracking.

  Aside from an instadeath, your biggest worry is a situation 
that spirals out of control.  It's easy to get into a situation 
that it's almost impossible to get out of.

  Jumping can help prevent that.




